Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;
register(MethodWriteT);
define
    mwA=2;
    mwB=3;
    mwC=4;
    mwH1;
    mwH2;
    mwH3;
    mwList;
    mwJux;
    mwBound;
    mwCtl;
    mwBad;
    mwLists code={
        mwH1 := mwA;
        mwH2 := mwB;
        mwH3 := mwC;
        mwList +% *mwH1;
        mwList +% *mwH2;
        mwList +% *mwH3;
        cerr "MW L3 " mwList.listLengtH:;
        mwJux +% mwA mwB mwC;
        cerr "MW LJ " mwJux.listLengtH:;
        };
    mwMethods code={
        mwBound.methoD = "testOP";
        cerr "MW M1 " mwBound.methoD:;
        cerr "MW I1 " mwBound.isMethoD:;
        cerr "MW M0 " mwCtl.methoD:;
        };
    mwRefuse code={
        mwBad.methoD = "mwNoSuchMethod";
        };
    ;
mwLists();
mwMethods();
mwRefuse();
cerr "MW MB " mwBad.methoD:;
cerr "METHODWRITE SENTINEL":;
stop();

methodWriteT -- Clod, 2026-10-09, for Tony's testListed in tester.

L3 is the control: three +% lines attach three. LJ is the one-line form with plain
names side by side; interpretXP hands +% its juxtaposition list xl1, and opAddAttribute
now finishes and attaches each term. Starred terms cannot be written this way:
*a *b *c reads as a * b * c (KANT-43 absorbs the binary star).

M1/I1: x.methoD = "name" binds the method dlsym finds by that text (accessorWriteMethod,
as ruleMethod does) and sets isMethod. M0 is the never-written control, so the 1 cannot
be a default. MB: a name dlsym cannot find is refused by name and binds nothing, read 0.
